"\n\n\n\n\n## Ordered\n\n\n## Review\nAn Italian restaurant located in Postal Lane, a storied alley next to the Melbourne GPO building.  \n\nSitting at an outdoor table in the laneway watching people pass by, we could soak in Melbourne's vibrant .  \n\nThe dishes we ordered were the signature chef-recommended  and .  \n\nThe presentation was great and the food tasted good overall, but it wasn't distinctly memorable enough to leave a strong impression — it felt a little ordinary.  \n\nIf anything, what stood out most that day was the Hawkers Pilsner, a local Melbourne craft beer I tried for the first time.  \n\nIts clean, crisp finish cut right through the richness of the food, and I loved it.  \nIt's a great spot to enjoy the vibes of a beautiful laneway and a cold local beer rather than the food itself.  \n## Pictures\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"